Full Text of Measure L
City of Placentia
AN ORDINANCE OF THE CITY OF PLACENTIA, CALIFORNIA, AMENDING SECTION 5.08.500 OF THE MUNICIPAL
CODE TO CHANGE THE RATE OF THE TRANSIENT OCCUPANCY TAX AND ADDING SECTION 3.20.100 TO THE
MUNICIPAL CODE TO REQUIRE CERTAIN ACCOUNTABILITY MEASURES
WHEREAS, Section 3.20.020 of the Placentia Municipal Code requires that, for the privilege of occupancy in any hotel, each transient is subject
to and shall pay a transient occupancy tax at the rate set forth in Section 5.08.500 of the Municipal Code; and
WHEREAS, the transient occupancy tax is collected by the hotel operator from the transient and then remitted by the operator to the City; and
WHEREAS, the transient occupancy tax is governed by Chapter 3.20 of the Municipal Code; and
WHEREAS, Section 3.20.010 of the Municipal Code provides that “transient” means any person who exercises occupancy or is entitled to
occupancy by reason of concession, permit, right of access, license or other agreement for a period of 30 consecutive calendar days or less, counting
portions of calendar days as full days and that any such person so occupying space in a hotel shall be deemed to be a transient until the period of
30 days has expired unless there is an agreement in writing between the operator and the occupant providing for a longer period of occupancy; and
WHEREAS, Section 3.20.010 of the Municipal Code provides that “hotel” means any structure, or any portion of any structure, which is occupied
or intended or designed for occupancy by transients for dwelling, lodging or sleeping purposes, and includes any hotel, inn, tourist home or house,
motel, studio motel, bachelor hotel, lodging house, rooming house, apartment house, dormitory, public or private club, mobile home or house trailer at
a fixed location, or other similar structure or portion thereof; and
WHEREAS, Section 3.20.010 of the Municipal Code provides that “rent” means the consideration charged, whether or not received, for the
occupancy of space in a hotel valued in money, whether to be received in money, goods, labor or otherwise, including all receipts, cash, credits and
property and services of any kind or nature, without any deduction therefrom whatsoever; and
WHEREAS, the rate of the Transient Occupancy Tax is currently 10%; and
WHEREAS, the People of the City of Placentia desire to increase the rate of the tax to 14%, and to adopt certain accountability measures.
NOW, THEREFORE, THE PEOPLE OF THE CITY OF PLACENTIA DO HEREBY ORDAIN AS FOLLOWS:
SECTION 1. Section 5.08.500 of Chapter 5.08 (Finance Department—Business Licenses) of the Municipal Code is hereby amended to read:
§ 5.08.500 Transient Occupancy Tax
The rate of the transient occupancy tax imposed by Section 3.20.020 of this Code is 14% of the rent charged by the operator.
SECTION 2. Section 3.20.100 is added to Chapter 3.20 (Transient Occupancy Tax) of the Municipal Code to read as follows:
§3.20.100 Accountability
A. The proceeds of the transient occupancy tax as well as the expenditure thereof, shall be audited annually by an independent accounting firm.
Such independent audit may be a part of any other independent audit of municipal finances. The report of the audit shall be filed with the City
Council and shall be a public record of the City.
B. The citizen’s oversight committee established by Section 3.32.020 of this code shall, in addition to its other duties, review the expenditure
of funds generated by the transient occupancy tax. It shall prepare an annual report on such expenditures which shall be presented to the
city council and shall also be published on the city’s webpage. Unless otherwise directed by resolution or ordinance of the city council, or
by Chapter 3.32 or other provision of this code, the committee shall not have any function, power, or authority other than those expressly
provided in this section. In no event shall a failure of the city council or the committee to meet, or to take any other action required by this
section, invalidate any tax imposed or collected under this chapter; however, any court of competent jurisdiction may issue an order to the city
compelling the city to comply with the requirements of this section.
C. The proceeds of the transient occupancy tax shall be deposited in the general fund of the city and may be used for any lawful municipal
purpose. The tax is a general tax imposed for general government purposes.
SECTION 3. The City Council may, by ordinance, amend this Ordinance. However, the City Council shall not increase the rate of the tax imposed by
this Ordinance above the rate set forth in this Ordinance without the approval of the increase by a vote of the Electorate.
SECTION 4. If any section, subsection, sentence, clause, or phrase of this Ordinance is held invalid, such decision shall not affect the validity of the
remaining provisions of this Ordinance.
SECTION 5. This Ordinance shall take effect on January 1, 2027.
