Argument in Favor of Measure L
Visitors Pay Their Fair Share, Residents Benefit.
Vote YES on Placentia’s Hotel Tax Measure to protect essential city
services, keep local dollars in Placentia, and ensure visitors pay their fair
share. Visitors Pay, Residents Benefit.
Placentia’s hotel tax is paid only by guests who stay in local hotels,
motels, and short-term rentals. It is not a tax on Placentia residents’
property, income, or everyday expenses.
This measure is a fair, common-sense way to increase revenue without
raising taxes on local residents. When visitors use Placentia’s roads,
public safety services, parks, and infrastructure, they should help pay to
maintain them.
Placentia’s current hotel tax rate has not kept pace with inflation
and is below other Orange County rates. Updating Placentia’s rate to
the proposed 14% will keep Placentia competitive for tourism while
generating approximately $715,000 each year with every dollar staying
in Placentia.
A YES vote also supports transparency and accountability. A Citizens’
Oversight Committee will prepare annual audits to ensure funds are used
to maintain the city’s infrastructure, including roads and parks; build fiscal
reserves; and support public safety.
The City continues to work hard to improve Placentia’s finances,
invest in public safety, and maintain neighborhood services despite
continuing cost increases. Without additional local revenue, the City
faces harder choices in the years ahead about what services can be
maintained.
This measure helps Placentia control its future because the money
stays local. It supports only local needs to protect the quality of life that
makes Placentia a safe, family-friendly community.
Please join residents, community leaders, and local taxpayers in voting
YES on Placentia’s Hotel Tax Measure.
